 The web tier drops one raw export per UTC day into data/pageviews/<YYYY-MM-DD>.csv
 at about 01:00 UTC the next morning. This DAG aggregates yesterday's file into
 the `daily_pageviews` table (views and unique visitors per page).
+
+Period contract
+---------------
+* Scheduled run firing at 03:00 UTC on day D  ->  processes day D-1 (UTC).
+  Example: run firing 2026-09-02 03:00 UTC  ->  reads 2026-09-01.csv and writes
+  view_date = 2026-09-01.
+* Backfill run for logical date D            ->  same window as scheduled run for D.
+* Rerun / clear of any run                   ->  same day as original (idempotent).
+* No data exists before 2026-09-01; the DAG will never be asked to load earlier.
+
+Timetable choice
+----------------
+CronDataIntervalTimetable keeps Airflow-2 interval semantics on Airflow 3:
+  data_interval_start = 2026-09-01 03:00 UTC  (D-1 at the cron hour)
+  data_interval_end   = 2026-09-02 03:00 UTC  (D at the cron hour)
+run_window() extracts [start, end) from those values.
+
+catchup=True + max_active_runs=1
+  catchup fills every missed interval since start_date, one run at a time.
+  max_active_runs=1 serialises runs so DuckDB (single-writer) is never contested.
 """
 
